<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Province of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a> formed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> from lands taken from the Kingdom of Saxony and older Prussian territories such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a>. Its capital was Magdeburg. It was divided in 1944, and its lands now lie mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/province-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Province of Saxony" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Preu%C3%9Fen_-_Provinz_Sachsen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
